(3604431, 504867, 77537, '<td valign="top">elegant photo real and fairy tale both. i''d have deepened the shadows with photoshop highlight/shadow function and warmed the color a bit; but gee that is a beautiful girl</td>', 'elegant photo real and fairy tale both. i''d have deepened the shadows with photoshop highlight/shadow function and warmed the color a bit; but gee that is a beautiful girl', '2007-05-02 06:51:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3604439, 505172, 43073, '<td valign="top">This image really appeals to me as a whole. The deep blues are fantastic, and the tones are warm and pleasing. The lack of sharpness of the reflection (which is where I see the symmetry here) decreases the effectiveness of the image in relation to the challenge topic for me. Also, being nitpicky here, the loss of blur on the boat (especially on the left), the thinness to the wires (perhaps due to resizing), and the "thing" on the right side over the post (near the tree) were elements that made this less effective for me.</td>', 'This image really appeals to me as a whole. The deep blues are fantastic, and the tones are warm and pleasing. The lack of sharpness of the reflection (which is where I see the symmetry here) decreases the effectiveness of the image in relation to the challenge topic for me. Also, being nitpicky here, the loss of blur on the boat (especially on the left), the thinness to the wires (perhaps due to resizing), and the "thing" on the right side over the post (near the tree) were elements that made this less effective for me.', '2007-05-02 06:56:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(3604442, 503352, 43073, '<td valign="top">Neat image, taken from the right perspective for the challenge, I think. I like the fade into darkness, and in those areas the apparent intentional oversharpening works pretty well. It works less well on the wires for me (the jaggies don''t appeal to me in the way the halos do), but given basic editing, you had to make a compromise somewhere!</td>', 'Neat image, taken from the right perspective for the challenge, I think. I like the fade into darkness, and in those areas the apparent intentional oversharpening works pretty well. It works less well on the wires for me (the jaggies don''t appeal to me in the way the halos do), but given basic editing, you had to make a compromise somewhere!', '2007-05-02 06:59:22.000000', NULL, 1),
