(3635396, 505599, 20462, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Shermy:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RPvanderHilst:</b></div><hr/><i> Apart from the Y-shape there really is no symmetry here.. -5- </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This made me laugh. It''s like saying about a portrait "apart from the person in this picture, it is not a portrait".<br/> <br/>Anyways, I thought the picture was creative :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Exactly...haha.  That''s what I thought.  To my discredit, I re-read the challenge descrip and it said "use symmetry to compose your photograph".....which I did not do at all.  So this is the one time, where I will freely admit, I screwed up....oh well.  There is symmetry, natural as a matter of fact, but not the whole image which I now feel was the point.</td>', 'Originally posted by Shermy: Originally posted by RPvanderHilst: Apart from the Y-shape there really is no symmetry here.. -5-   This made me laugh. It''s like saying about a portrait "apart from the person in this picture, it is not a portrait". Anyways, I thought the picture was creative :)   Exactly...haha.  That''s what I thought.  To my discredit, I re-read the challenge descrip and it said "use symmetry to compose your photograph".....which I did not do at all.  So this is the one time, where I will freely admit, I screwed up....oh well.  There is symmetry, natural as a matter of fact, but not the whole image which I now feel was the point.', '2007-05-09 23:13:11.000000', NULL, 0),
