(3655268, 504628, 39057, '<td valign="top">Hahn23...why did you not just comment on the merits of the pictuer? Why comment on what you feel was "trying to influence the voting". Why throw in the 104 place finish? <br/> <br/>You also say the photographer is trying to drag down others...<br/> <br/>Do you remember the <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_results.php?CHALLENGE_ID=620" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Wildlife III Challenge?</a> You made many, many rude remarks about people taking "zoo shots". IMO you were trying to bring down the competition. You felt that your "wild" shots were somehow "better" only because they were "not zoo shots". Your comment on the winner of the Wildlife III shot was purely ridiculous. <br/> <br/>With all of your "zoo shot" comments...you have NO RIGHT to challenge this photographer.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> Too bad you tried to influence the voting of others by trashing the LLR and FM images. Congratulations on your 104th place "win".  My advice is to present your best effort to the challenges, and then try to avoid the attempts to drag down others in an effort to somehow lift your own.  Is your "knock down" approach the way of the Netherlands?. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-05-16 17:56:50.</i></td>', 'Hahn23...why did you not just comment on the merits of the pictuer? Why comment on what you feel was "trying to influence the voting". Why throw in the 104 place finish?  You also say the photographer is trying to drag down others... Do you remember the Wildlife III Challenge? You made many, many rude remarks about people taking "zoo shots". IMO you were trying to bring down the competition. You felt that your "wild" shots were somehow "better" only because they were "not zoo shots". Your comment on the winner of the Wildlife III shot was purely ridiculous.  With all of your "zoo shot" comments...you have NO RIGHT to challenge this photographer. Originally posted by hahn23: Too bad you tried to influence the voting of others by trashing the LLR and FM images. Congratulations on your 104th place "win".  My advice is to present your best effort to the challenges, and then try to avoid the attempts to drag down others in an effort to somehow lift your own.  Is your "knock down" approach the way of the Netherlands?. ', '2007-05-16 10:39:53.000000', '2007-05-16 18:56:50.000000', 0),
